# Everything in this repo is text, and it is LF everywhere.
#
# Why this file exists: line-ending behaviour is controlled by core.autocrlf,
# which is a *global*, per-machine git setting (currently `input` on this
# laptop). A per-machine setting fixes one surface and leaves every other one
# alone — this repo is reachable from Claude Code on the laptop, from Cowork,
# and from claude.ai/code against the GitHub mirror. The rule belongs to the
# repo, not to a machine.
#
# Under CRLF, a .sh file's shebang breaks silently, and any byte-level
# comparison starts reporting differences that are not really there.
*       text=auto eol=lf
